  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1156 PM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nA cold front will approach the area from the north Saturday\nevening and overnight, with shower and thunderstorm chances\nspreading into parts of northeast Oklahoma by late evening into\nthe overnight hours. As the cold front sags south into our area\nduring the day Sunday, additional showers and storms will form in\nits vicinity by afternoon, with an isolated severe storm or two\npossible. Shower and storm chances will continue Sunday night into\nMonday as the front continues to progress southeast across the\narea.\n\nMuch cooler temperatures will prevail next week in the wake of the\nfront, with temperatures much closer to the seasonal averages. A\nfew showers may drift into parts of northeast Oklahoma from time\nto time later next week, but most places will remain dry.",
